    {
      "anchor": "extending",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Extending"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "post--subscriptions-id-action-?do=extend",
      "kind": "operation",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/api/2.0/subscriptions/{id}/action/?do=extend"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "extending",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "200 OK – no error"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "extending",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Extends the subscription. An extended subscription is actually just another subscription that is linked to the original If a period or and end_time are specified in the request,they are used. If neither are specified, the creation length of the subscription is used."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "extending",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "A caveat to this is that a subscription created initially with an end_time, the exact interval is used. Subscriptions that are created with a period have the period parsed again in the context of the new start_time. An example would be a subscription created on the 1st of February with a period of ‘1 month’ will be extended for 31 days, but one that was created with an end date of 1st of March will be extended for 28 days."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "extending",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "If the specified subscription has actually been extended, it traverses and extends the last subscription in the chain."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "autorenewing",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Autorenewing"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "post--subscriptions-id-action-?do=auto_renew",
      "kind": "operation",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/api/2.0/subscriptions/{id}/action/?do=auto_renew"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "autorenewing",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Toggles the autorenew flag of the subscription. Optionally, the value can be specified in the request."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "autorenewing",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "200 OK – no error"
    },
